%% Bunny OS Phase 1 — Diagram 7 (file 12): Local-to-Cloud Escalation
%% How Bunny determines local resources are insufficient, explains the change,
%% obtains consent, minimizes context, and invokes an external provider.
%% All seven disclosure duties are discharged and each is labelled below.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SH as Bunny Shell
    participant PE as Plan Engine
    participant CR as Capability Router
    participant HCS as Hardware Capability Service
    participant LIM as Local Inference Manager
    participant BS as Budget Service
    participant MEM as Memory Service
    participant POL as Policy Engine
    participant GL as Grant Ledger
    participant PA as Provider Adapters
    participant AUD as Audit Service

    PE->>CR: route request for step 4<br/>task class refactor, 11 steps remaining

    CR->>HCS: current capability profile
    HCS-->>CR: 16GB RAM, 89GB/s bandwidth,<br/>on battery, thermal headroom low
    CR->>LIM: local tier fit for this task class
    LIM-->>CR: 20B MoE loaded, but multi-step<br/>agentic reliability below threshold

    CR->>CR: evaluate against workspace routing posture
    Note over CR: posture is "balanced" — escalation<br/>permitted with per-workspace consent.<br/>A "privacy-strict" posture would stop here<br/>and offer degrade or decline instead.

    CR->>BS: estimate for hosted route
    BS-->>CR: 40-80 calls, est. 0.60 to 1.10,<br/>workspace budget 5.00 remaining

    CR->>MEM: minimize context for this step
    MEM-->>CR: 3 records in scope,<br/>2 sensitive-class records EXCLUDED
    Note over MEM: sensitive classes are excluded from<br/>provider context by default (§10 privacy floor)

    CR-->>PE: recommend escalation + explanation record
    PE->>POL: action class 9 — send externally
    POL-->>PE: ESCALATE — requires explicit consent

    PE->>SH: escalation disclosure
    Note over SH: the seven duties, all rendered:<br/>1 why · 2 what leaves · 3 minimized context<br/>4 named destination · 5 cost · 6 consent level<br/>7 audit record will be written
    SH->>U: "Local model can't reliably carry an<br/>11-step refactor. Send this file and the<br/>plan to Anthropic? Est. 0.60-1.10."

    alt user approves
        U->>SH: approve for this plan
        SH->>GL: grant (class 9, scope=this plan, duration=until complete)
        GL->>AUD: grant issued
        CR->>PA: invoke hosted route
        PA->>AUD: egress record — what left, to whom, under which grant
        PA-->>CR: response
        Note over PA,CR: response is UNTRUSTED INPUT —<br/>it may propose, never authorize
        CR->>BS: actual cost
        BS->>BS: reconcile forecast against actual
        SH->>U: route chip changes to<br/>"Anthropic · metered · leaves this device"
    else user declines
        U->>SH: keep it local
        SH->>PE: degrade or decline
        PE->>PE: replan within local capability<br/>and state the limitation plainly
        Note over PE: C11 — Bunny says the work is<br/>narrower, it does not silently<br/>produce a worse result
    end
